  "reconstructionNotes": "Two-zone layout. Left zone: thin black axes with arrowheads, a thick sky-blue unit circle centered on the origin, red/salmon radius and tangent-ray lines, three solid red dots at (1,0), (cos x, sin x), (1, tan x), dashed red segments for the vertical tangent leg and the chord, a small curved angle arrow labeled x at the origin, and a curly brace labeled 1 under the unit base. Right zone: three shapes in a row, all sharing base length 1 and left-vertex angle x, filled pale pink with red outlines; the first is the tall right triangle (vertical leg labeled tan x) with a blue dashed arc crossing it, the second is the sector with a solid blue arc as its curved edge, the third is the short triangle with a blue dashed arc bulging just outside it and a curly brace labeled sin x on the right. Below the three shapes, two centered text rows: 'Area of triangle ≥ Area of sector ≥ Area of triangle' and beneath it the stacked fractions 'tan x / 2 ≥ x / 2 ≥ sin x / 2'. In overlaid mode, draw all three shapes concentric on a single left-vertex with graded pink opacities so the nesting reads clearly, keeping the blue arc for the sector boundary. Panel labels are clickable and should glow / desaturate the others when selected. Include a small readout box giving current x, tan x/2, x/2, sin x/2, and sin x / x. Palette: sky blue for circle/arcs, salmon-red for all straight construction lines and dots, pale pink fills, black text and axes."
}

